  <id value="consent-example-No-Emergency"/>
  <text>
    <status value="generated"/>
    <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
      <p>Withhold Authorization for Treatment and for Emergency Treatment</p>
      <p>Patient "Jacen Solo" wishes to have no data at the Burgers University Medical Center available and not allow Emergency treatment use.
        An overall Deny consent Directive, with an "Deny" of purposeOfUse "TREAT" and "Deny" purposeOfUse "ETREAT". </p>
      <p>This example uses the ETREAT purpose-of-use code for emergency treatment. Implementations may also need other purpose-of-use codes, such as BTG or Disaster-related codes, to represent local break-glass or disaster-access policies.</p>
    </div>
  </text>
